    "rules": "==================================================\n\nSUPPORTED FORMATS:\n- 1v1\n- 1v1v1v1 Tournament\n- 2v2\n- 1v2 / 2v1\n- 1v3 / 3v1\n\n\nCORE 1v1 RULES\n\nEach player gets 3 valid attacking possessions.\n\nAttacker:\n- Begins around midfield with ball.\n\nDefender:\n- Begins in a region near the goal.\n- May challenge.\n- Save.\n- Clear.\n- Defend normally.\n\nA possession only counts as an official attempt once:\n- Attacker scores, OR\n- Defender touches the ball.\n\nIf attacker completely misses and defender never touches the ball:\n- Do not consume an attempt.\n- Reset and retry that possession.\n\nScoring:\n- Attacker goal = 1 point.\n- Defender save/clear/touch that stops the scoring attack = 0 attacker points.\n\nAfter first player completes 3 valid attacks:\n- Switch attacker/defender roles.\n\nWinner:\nMost attacking goals.\n\n1v1 Tie:\nEach gets 1 additional attacking possession.\nIf one scores and the other does not:\n- scorer wins.\nIf both score or both fail:\n- repeat paired extra possessions until separated.\n\n\nBROWSER — 1v1\n\nUse normal rules screen.\n\nNo detailed per-possession browser tracking is required.\nPlayers can manually keep score.\n\nAt end:\n- Host selects winner.\n- No Draw option because overtime continues until separation.\n\nProvide:\n- \"Redo / Restart Battle\" in host recovery menu if setup is accidentally broken.\n\n\n1v1v1v1 — TOURNAMENT VERSION\n\nUse Global Tournament Bracket System.\n\nEvery mini-match uses the exact 1v1 Beat the Defender rules above.\n\nSemifinals:\n- simultaneous.\n\nFinal / 3rd:\n- Host chooses simultaneous or sequential.\n\nEach mini-match resolves its own Beat the Defender tiebreak before being marked complete.\n\nDo not try to create a four-player rotating-attacker version.\nThis is explicitly tournament style.\n\n\n2v2 — TEAM BEAT THE DEFENDER\n\nTwo attackers play together against two defenders.\n\nEach TEAM gets:\n- 3 valid attacking possessions.\n\nOn an attacking possession:\n- Both teammates may participate in offense.\n- Both defenders defend normally.\n\nPossession counts when:\n- Attacking team scores, OR\n- Defending team makes defensive contact that stops/redirects the attack.\n\nUntouched complete miss:\n- Retry.\n- Do not consume possession.\n\nAttacking team goal:\n1 point.\n\nAfter one team completes 3 valid attacking possessions:\n- Switch team roles.\n\nWinner:\nTeam with more successful attacking goals.\n\nTie:\nEach team gets 1 additional attacking possession.\nRepeat paired extra possessions until one team scores in a tiebreak round where the other does not.\n\nBrowser:\nDefault Team A / Team B result screen after completion.\nNo Draw.\n\n\n1v2 / 2v1 — TAG-TEAM BEAT THE DEFENDER\n\nSolo:\nAlways the Defender.\n\nDuo:\nBoth players take separate attacking turns.\n\nEach Duo member gets:\n3 valid attacking possessions.\n\nTherefore:\n6 total valid attacking possessions for the Duo.\n\nUse same valid-attempt rule:\n- Goal counts as an attempt.\n- Solo defensive touch/save/clear counts as an attempt.\n- Untouched complete miss does not consume attempt.\n\nTrack conceptually:\n- Team Scores\nversus\n- Solo Saves.\n\nIf more Team Scores than Solo Saves:\nDuo wins.\n\nIf more Solo Saves than Team Scores:\nSolo wins.\n\nIf equal:\nDraw.\n\nBrowser:\nPlayers may track the individual attempts themselves.\nAt end give Host:\n- Solo Won\n- Duo Won\n- Draw\n\nDo NOT force overtime because this variant explicitly allows a draw.\n\n\n1v3 / 3v1 — TAG-TEAM BEAT THE DEFENDER\n\nSame as 1v2 except:\n\nSolo:\nAlways Defender.\n\nEach Trio player:\n3 attacking possessions.\n\nTotal:\n9 valid attacks.\n\nCompare:\n- Team Scores\n- Solo Saves\n\nMore Team Scores:\nTrio wins.\n\nMore Saves:\nSolo wins.\n\nEqual:\nDraw.\n\nBrowser:\nHost selects result.\n\n\n=================================================="
