    "rules": "==================================================\n\nSUPPORTED FORMATS:\n- 1v1\n- 1v1v1\n- 1v1v1v1\n- 2v2\n\nNOTE:\nTwo-Headed HORSE and Three-Headed HORSE are separate Challenge concepts and will be documented separately later.\n\n\nCORE HORSE RULES\n\nThis is a 2-letter elimination version of HORSE.\n\nEach player starts:\n0 / 2 letters.\n\nBrowser randomly creates a turn order when applicable.\n\nCurrent Setter:\nVerbally calls exact freestyle shot/mechanic.\n\nSetter gets:\n1 attempt.\n\nIf Setter MISSES:\n- Nobody gets a letter.\n- Move to next active Setter in turn order.\n\nIf Setter MAKES called shot:\n- Required Copier(s) each get exactly 1 attempt.\n\nCopier succeeds:\n- No letter.\n\nCopier fails:\n- +1 letter.\n\nAt 2 letters:\n- Player is eliminated.\n\nIMPORTANT SETTER RULE:\nAfter somebody successfully sets a shot, that person does NOT immediately set again.\nProceed to the next eligible active Setter in browser turn order.\n\nEliminated players:\n- Removed from future setter rotation.\n- Removed from future copying requirements.\n\n\n1v1\n\nRandom starting Setter.\n\nSetter miss:\nSwitch Setter.\n\nSetter make:\nOpponent gets 1 copy.\n\nFailed copy:\n+1 letter.\n\n2 letters:\nLose.\n\nBrowser UI SHOULD track this Challenge because letters/turn order can become confusing.\n\nRecommended active UI:\n- Current Setter highlighted.\n- Both players' letter count visible.\n- Host buttons:\n  - Setter Missed\n  - Setter Made\n\nIf Setter Made:\nShow copier resolution:\n- [Player] Copied\n- [Player] Failed Copy\n\nHost records result.\n\nFailed copy:\nBrowser automatically adds letter.\n\nBefore moving to next setter:\nbriefly show updated letter state.\n\nHost gets:\nUndo Last HORSE Action\n\nUndo should reverse only most recent recorded made/missed/letter event.\n\n\n1v1v1\n\nRandom turn order for 3 players.\n\nSetter makes:\nEVERY OTHER active player must attempt the copy once.\n\nExample:\nA sets successfully.\nB and C each copy once.\n\nEach failed copier:\n+1 letter independently.\n\nIMPORTANT:\nResolve every required copier before starting next Setter turn.\n\nIf multiple players reach 2 letters from the same successful Set:\nThey are eliminated on the same turn and SHARE the same placement.\n\nContinue until:\n1 player remains.\n\nFinal survivor:\n1st.\n\nElimination order determines lower placements.\nSame-turn eliminations share placement.\n\nBrowser:\nTrack:\n- Turn order\n- Current setter\n- Letters\n- Eliminated players\n- Shared-placement elimination batch\n\n\n1v1v1v1\n\nSame FFA system with 4 players.\n\nSuccessful Setter:\nAll other active players copy once.\n\nContinue until one survivor.\n\nSame-turn eliminations share placement.\n\n\n2v2 — TEAM HORSE\n\nAll 4 players have INDIVIDUAL letter counts.\n\nBrowser randomly creates one turn order across all 4 players.\n\nSetter:\nCalls and attempts shot.\n\nSetter miss:\nMove to next active player.\n\nSetter make:\nONLY active players from OPPOSING TEAM must copy.\n\nSetter's teammate does NOT copy.\n\nExample:\nA1 sets successfully.\nA2 does nothing.\nB1 and B2 each get one copy attempt.\n\nFailed opposing copier:\n+1 individual letter.\n\nAt 2 letters:\nThat individual is eliminated.\n\nAn eliminated teammate stays out.\nTheir surviving teammate may continue alone.\n\nContinue until:\nOnly one team has at least one active surviving player.\n\nThat team wins.\n\nThis Challenge cannot end merely because one individual is last among their team; they may carry the team alone.\n\nBrowser:\nDisplay team grouping clearly while still showing individual letter counters.\n\nTurn order:\nSkip eliminated players automatically.\n\nUndo:\nHost may undo last recorded HORSE action.\n\n\nANTI-CHEAT / HUMAN-JUDGMENT NOTE\n\nThe browser does NOT judge whether the verbal call was actually completed correctly.\n\nPlayers decide that themselves.\nHost only records:\n- made\n- missed\n- copied\n- failed copy\n\n\n=================================================="
