    "rules": "==================================================\n\nSUPPORTED FORMATS:\n- 1v1\n- 1v1v1\n- 1v1v1v1\n- 2v2\n- 1v2 / 2v1\n- 1v3 / 3v1\n\n\nCORE TRAINING RULES\n\nEvery participant uses:\nThe exact same Custom Training pack.\n\nObjective:\nComplete shots 1 through 10 IN ORDER.\n\nRules:\n- Start on shot #1.\n- May retry missed shot as many times as necessary.\n- Must successfully score current shot before proceeding.\n- No skipping.\n- Challenge progress ends after completing shot #10.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n1v1 — TRAINING PACK SPRINT\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nNo overall browser timer is required.\n\nBoth players race simultaneously.\n\nFirst player to complete shot #10:\nWins.\n\nIf players cannot tell who finished first:\nThey may agree to redo the final comparison/run as necessary.\n\nBrowser:\nUse normal result screen.\n\nOptionally show a simple:\n\"Ready?\"\nHost Start\n\nbut browser does not need to know individual shot progression.\n\nDo not force browser-side shot buttons unless desired later.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n1v1v1 — TRAINING PACK SPRINT\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nAll 3 race simultaneously.\n\nFinish order determines placements:\n\nFirst to complete #10:\n1st.\n\nSecond:\n2nd.\n\nThird:\n3rd.\n\nBrowser SHOULD provide a lightweight finish-registration system to reduce arguments.\n\nRecommended:\n\nEach player has:\nFINISHED button.\n\nWhen pressed:\nStore authoritative server timestamp to millisecond precision.\n\nDisplay:\n\"Finish submitted\"\n\nDo not allow players to repeatedly overwrite their finish time.\n\nIf player accidentally presses early:\nHost may:\nInvalidate Finish\n\nThat returns the player to active state.\n\nUse finish timestamps to rank.\n\nIf two timestamps are genuinely tied at browser precision:\nThose players may share placement or Host may resolve based on actual visible finish.\nPrefer Host correction if players clearly know who finished first.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n1v1v1v1 — TRAINING PACK SPRINT\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nSame as 1v1v1 with 4 players.\n\nRank finish timestamps:\n1st–4th.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n2v2 — TRAINING PACK SPRINT\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nAll 4 players race individually through shots 1–10.\n\nThe FIRST individual from either team to complete shot #10:\nWins the entire Challenge for their team.\n\nTeammate does not also need to finish.\n\nExample:\nA1 finishes first.\nEven if A2 is last:\nTeam A wins immediately.\n\nBrowser:\nUse same FINISHED timestamp system.\n\nAs soon as first valid finish occurs:\nPause briefly.\nShow:\n\"[Player] finished first — Team A wins.\"\n\nHost should have:\nCorrect Finish\nbefore rewards in case someone accidentally pressed Finish early.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n1v2 / 2v1 — TIMED AVERAGE VERSION\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nThis version is NOT simply \"first to finish.\"\n\nEvery participant gets an individual timed run.\n\nEach participant:\nCompletes shots 1–10.\n\nTimer:\nStarts at 0.0.\nCounts upward.\n\nEach player has their own separate run/time.\n\nThe browser decides run order unless the Host restarts/reorders before first run.\n\nFor the active player's run:\n\nSTART RUN\n→ stopwatch begins.\n\nPlayer completes shots 1–10.\n\nPlayer presses:\nSTOP TIMER\n\nBrowser freezes time.\n\nThen show:\n\nSUBMIT TIME\nREDO RUN\n\nSUBMIT TIME:\nLocks that player's official time.\n\nREDO RUN:\nDeletes that run and allows the same player to start again.\n\nThere is no hard redo limit.\nThis exists for:\n- Technical problems\n- Wrong pack\n- Accidental timer start\n- Other obvious mishaps\n\nOnce player submits official time and another player begins:\nHost may still correct/reopen the prior run through Host recovery if genuinely necessary.\n\nAfter:\nSolo\nDuo A\nDuo B\n\nall have official times:\n\nDuo Average =\n(Duo A Time + Duo B Time) / 2\n\nCompare:\nSolo Time\nvs\nDuo Average\n\nLower:\nWins.\n\nExact equal:\nDraw unless players voluntarily redo;\nhowever exact equality at timer precision is extremely unlikely.\n\nDisplay calculation clearly.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n1v3 / 3v1 — TIMED AVERAGE VERSION\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nSame timed-run system.\n\nOfficial runs:\nSolo\nTrio A\nTrio B\nTrio C\n\nTrio Average =\n(A + B + C) / 3\n\nCompare:\nSolo Time vs Trio Average.\n\nLower time:\nWins.\n\nIf exact equality:\nDraw.\n\nBROWSER:\nShow each official run to at least 0.1 seconds.\nInternal timestamp precision can be finer.\n\nDo not round each player's time before averaging.\nAverage full stored times, then round only for display.\n\n\n=================================================="
