    "rules": "==================================================\n\nSUPPORTED FORMATS:\n- 1v1\n- 1v1v1v1 Tournament\n- 2v2\n- 1v2 / 2v1 Tag-Team\n- 1v3 / 3v1 Tag-Team\n\n\nCORE RULES\n\nPlayers must perform active gameplay in reverse.\n\nIMPORTANT EXCEPTION:\nKickoff does NOT have to be reverse-only.\n\nAfter kickoff:\nIntentional normal forward driving is prohibited.\n\nAllowed while playing reverse:\n- Steering\n- Wavedashing\n- Normal reverse-based control\n- Other legal movement that does not involve intentionally driving normally forward\n\nPlayers may still:\n- Jump\n- Flip\n- Boost as appropriate\nas long as the actual movement rule remains reverse-focused.\n\nThe browser does not police movement.\nPlayers enforce this rule themselves.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n1v1 — REVERSE 1v1\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nMatch:\n2 minutes.\n\nMost goals:\nWins.\n\nTie:\nContinue with Reverse rules.\nNext valid goal wins.\n\nBrowser:\nDefault result selection.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n1v1v1v1 — REVERSE 1v1 TOURNAMENT\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nUse Global Tournament System.\n\nEach mini-match:\n2-minute Reverse 1v1.\n\nTie:\nNext goal under Reverse rules.\n\nSemis:\nSimultaneous.\n\nFinal + 3rd:\nHost chooses simultaneous or sequential.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n2v2 — REVERSE 2v2\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nMatch:\n3 minutes.\n\nAll 4 players use Reverse restriction.\n\nMost team goals:\nWins.\n\nTie:\nNext valid goal wins.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n1v2 / 2v1 — TAG-TEAM REVERSE\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nSolo plays:\nDuo A for 1 minute.\nDuo B for 1 minute.\n\nReverse rules apply to every segment.\n\nSolo goals:\nAdd across both segments.\n\nDuo goals:\nAdd A + B segments.\n\nHigher combined side score:\nWins.\n\nTie after both segments:\nNext-goal tiebreak.\n\nBrowser randomly selects one Duo member for tiebreak 1v1 against Solo.\n\nTiebreak remains Reverse rules.\n\nNext goal:\nWins.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n1v3 / 3v1 — TAG-TEAM REVERSE\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nSolo plays:\nEach Trio member for 1 minute.\n\n3 total segments.\n\nAdd:\nSolo's goals across all 3.\nTrio players' combined goals.\n\nHigher:\nWins.\n\nTie:\nBrowser randomly chooses one Trio player.\nNext-goal Reverse 1v1 tiebreak against Solo.\n\n\nBROWSER TAG-TEAM UI\n\nShow:\nSegment X / N\nSolo vs [Current Opponent]\n\nAfter each 1-minute mini-match:\nHost enters:\n- Solo Goals\n- Team Member Goals\n\nAllow:\nCorrect Segment Score\n\nThen advance.\n\nDo not reveal/change the underlying variant because Reverse remains fixed the entire Challenge.\n\n\n=================================================="
