    "rules": "==================================================\n\nSUPPORTED FORMATS:\n- 1v1\n- 1v1v1v1 Tournament\n- 2v2\n- 1v2 / 2v1 Tag-Team\n- 1v3 / 3v1 Tag-Team\n\n\nCORE RULE\n\nUse a randomly selected APPROVED built-in Rocket League/private-match game mode.\n\nNo:\n- Workshop maps\n- PC-only custom content\n- External mod requirements\n\nBrowser may choose from the approved game-mode pool and display the result.\n\nPlayers manually configure Rocket League.\n\nThe browser does NOT control the Rocket League lobby.\n\nExamples of eligible mode types may include approved native modes already supported by the game.\n\nDo not hardcode an unverified mode list in scattered components.\nUse one central approved mode pool.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n1v1 — RANDOM GAME MODE 1v1\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nBrowser:\nRandomly selects 1 approved mode.\n\nDisplay it clearly.\n\nPlayers configure mode manually.\n\nStandard target length:\n2 minutes\n\nunless the selected mode logically requires equivalent native scoring/ending behavior.\n\nWinner:\nDetermined by the selected mode's normal scoring/win rules.\n\nTie:\nNext valid scoring event under that mode unless that mode has a more appropriate native tiebreak.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n1v1v1v1 — RANDOM GAME MODE 1v1 TOURNAMENT\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nThis is the tournament adaptation of the Random Game Mode 1v1 Challenge.\n\nUse Global Tournament System.\n\nEach MINI-MATCH:\nReceives its own random approved game mode.\n\nDo NOT reveal Final/3rd-place modes during semifinals.\n\nSemifinal modes:\nReveal when semis begin.\n\nAfter both semis:\nRandomly generate/reveal:\n- Final mode\n- 3rd-place mode\n\nDuplicates:\nAllowed.\n\nA mode used in a semifinal may appear again later.\n\nEach mini-match uses normal Random Game Mode 1v1 winner logic.\n\n\nIMPORTANT:\nThis is different from the separate \"Random Game Mode Tournament\" concept documented later where PLAYERS choose the game mode.\nHere, the game mode is still randomly selected as part of this Challenge.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n2v2 — RANDOM GAME MODE 2v2\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nBrowser selects:\n1 approved mode.\n\nBoth teams use that same mode.\n\nTarget match length:\n3 minutes where appropriate.\n\nIf selected native mode uses a different natural win structure:\nUse that mode's proper result.\n\nWinner:\nTeam that wins selected game mode.\n\nTie:\nUse mode-appropriate next scoring event.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n1v2 / 2v1 — TAG-TEAM RANDOM GAME MODE\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nBrowser selects:\nONE random approved game mode for the ENTIRE Tag-Team Challenge.\n\nDo NOT reroll a different mode between opponents.\n\nPlayers manually configure/use that same mode for each mini-match.\n\nSegments:\nSolo vs Duo A = 1 minute\nSolo vs Duo B = 1 minute\n\nUse selected mode's scoring.\n\nAdd equivalent side scoring across segments.\n\nHigher combined side result:\nWins.\n\nIf tied:\nBrowser randomly selects one Duo player for tiebreak against Solo.\n\nTiebreak:\nSame selected game mode.\n\nUse next valid scoring event.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n1v3 / 3v1 — TAG-TEAM RANDOM GAME MODE\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nSame:\nOne random mode for whole Challenge.\n\n3 one-minute mini-matches.\n\nSolo participates in all.\nEach Trio member participates once.\n\nCombine scores.\n\nTie:\nRandom Trio member faces Solo in next-score tiebreak using same mode.\n\n\nBROWSER SAFETY\n\nBefore gameplay begins:\nAllow Host:\nREROLL MODE\n\nONLY before first mini-match begins.\n\nReason:\nIf random mode is unavailable/problematic.\n\nUse confirmation:\n\"Reroll the selected mode for the entire Challenge?\"\n\nOnce first mini-match starts:\nDo not casually reroll.\n\nRequire full Challenge restart if changing mode.\n\n\n=================================================="
