    "rules": "==================================================\n\nSUPPORTED FORMATS:\n- 1v1\n- 1v1v1v1 Tournament\n- 2v2\n\n\nCORE RULES\n\nAttack and defense alternate.\n\nAttacker begins:\nAround their own side of midfield.\n\nDefender:\nPlays normally.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nBOUNCE LIMIT\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nOnce attack begins:\n\nBall may touch ground:\nAT MOST ONCE.\n\nSecond ground touch:\nImmediately ends attempt.\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nA defender saving/clearing the ball does NOT automatically end the attempt.\n\nThe attacker may continue trying to recover and score as long as:\n- Possession remains playable\nAND\n- Ball has not exceeded the one-ground-bounce limit.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nSCORING\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nGoal with:\n0 ground bounces\n= 2 points\n\nGoal with:\nExactly 1 ground bounce\n= 1 point\n\nSecond ground bounce:\n= 0 points and attempt ends.\n\nNo goal:\n= 0.\n\n\n==================================================\n1v1 — ONE-BOUNCE ATTACK\n==================================================\n\nEach player:\n3 attacking possessions.\n\nAfter first player's 3:\nSwitch roles.\n\nHighest total points:\nWins.\n\nTie:\nEach player gets 1 extra attacking possession.\n\nAfter both extra possessions:\nCompare.\n\nIf tied:\nRepeat paired extra possessions until separated.\n\nBrowser:\nPlayers may track points manually.\n\nDefault result screen after completion.\n\n\n==================================================\n1v1v1v1 — TOURNAMENT VERSION\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT create a four-player rotating version.\n\nUse Global Tournament System.\n\nEvery mini-match:\nNormal 1v1 One-Bounce Attack.\n\nSemis:\nSimultaneous.\n\nFinal / 3rd:\nHost chooses simultaneous or sequential.\n\nEach mini-match resolves its own One-Bounce tiebreak before result is submitted.\n\n\n==================================================\n2v2 — TEAM ONE-BOUNCE ATTACK\n==================================================\n\nBoth teammates attack together.\n\nBoth opposing teammates defend together.\n\nEach TEAM receives:\n3 attacking possessions.\n\nThe one-bounce restriction applies to the BALL globally during that team possession.\n\nIt is NOT one bounce per attacking teammate.\n\nTeam Goal:\n0 bounces = 2\n1 bounce = 1\n2nd bounce = attempt ends / 0\n\nDefenders may:\n- Save\n- Clear\n- Challenge\nnormally.\n\nA save/clear does not end possession by itself.\n\nAfter Team A completes 3 attacks:\nSwitch.\n\nHigher team points:\nWins.\n\nTie:\nEach team gets 1 extra possession.\n\nRepeat paired team possessions until separated.\n\n\n=================================================="
