    "rules": "==================================================\n\nSUPPORTED FORMATS:\n- 1v1\n- 1v1v1v1 Tournament\n- 2v2\n\n\nCORE OBJECTIVE\n\nScore while attacking under three different possession timers.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nREQUIRED TIME VALUES\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n15 seconds:\nGoal = 1 point\n\n10 seconds:\nGoal = 2 points\n\n5 seconds:\nGoal = 3 points\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nGENERAL ATTACK RULES\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nEach attacking possession:\nBegins at center / kickoff position.\n\nDefender:\nPlays normally.\n\nAttacker may continue after:\n- Save\n- Clear\n- Defensive touch\n\nas long as time remains.\n\nThe attack only ends when:\n- Goal is scored.\n- Time reaches 0.\n- Attacker voluntarily ends turn.\n\n\nGOAL TIMING\n\nBall must FULLY cross goal line before timer expires.\n\nIf timer hits 0 before ball fully crosses:\n0 points.\n\n\n==================================================\n1v1 — PRESSURE SHOT CLOCK\n==================================================\n\nBrowser randomly selects:\nWho attacks first.\n\nEach player must complete:\n- One 15-second possession.\n- One 10-second possession.\n- One 5-second possession.\n\nPlayers are responsible for making sure they perform all three durations.\n\nBrowser should NOT permanently disable a duration button after use.\n\nReason:\nPlayers may need to redo a timer because of:\n- Setup issue\n- Misclick\n- Wrong start\n- Technical problem\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nACTIVE ATTACKER TIMER UI\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nOnly current Attacker receives active timer controls:\n\nSTART 15s\nSTART 10s\nSTART 5s\n\nOnce one is pressed:\n\n- Start synchronized countdown.\n- Show timer to EVERYONE.\n- Disable other Start buttons while current timer is running.\n\nAt 0:\nPlay clear end-of-attempt alert sound.\n\nAlso provide:\nRESTART TIMER\n\nduring setup/recovery as reasonable.\n\nAnd:\nEND TURN\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nEND TURN\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nWhen current attacker presses End Turn:\n\nPopup:\n\n\"HAVE YOU COMPLETED ALL THREE TIME LIMITS?\"\n\nYES\nNO\n\nNO:\nReturn to timer selection.\n\nYES:\nLock that player's normal attacking turn and switch roles.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nSCORING\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nPlayers manually keep track of points.\n\nBrowser does not need to ask:\n\"Did you score?\"\n\nunless later desired.\n\nAfter both players finish:\nHost chooses winner.\n\nTie:\nRepeat paired short-pressure possessions until separated.\n\nFor tiebreak:\nPlayers may verbally agree which time limit to use for the paired tiebreak.\nIf no special choice is made, use 5 seconds as default tiebreak pressure.\n\n\n==================================================\n1v1v1v1 — PRESSURE SHOT CLOCK TOURNAMENT\n==================================================\n\nUse Global Tournament System.\n\nEach mini-match:\nNormal 1v1 Pressure Shot Clock.\n\nSemis:\nSimultaneous.\n\nIMPORTANT TIMER IMPLEMENTATION:\n\nEach semifinal needs its own independent timer state.\n\nSemifinal A's 10-second timer must NOT affect Semifinal B.\n\nPlayers only see/control timer for their current matchup.\n\nAfter semis:\nFinal/3rd use fresh timer states.\n\nHost chooses simultaneous or sequential.\n\n\n==================================================\n2v2 — TEAM PRESSURE SHOT CLOCK\n==================================================\n\nEntire team attacks together.\n\nOpposing team defends together.\n\nEach TEAM performs:\n15s attack\n10s attack\n5s attack\n\nScoring:\nSame:\n15 = 1\n10 = 2\n5 = 3\n\nAttacking team's possession continues through saves/clears while time remains.\n\nBrowser timer flow:\nSame as 1v1.\n\nDuring Team A's turn:\nBoth attacking teammates may see timer controls.\n\nThe first valid Start press atomically starts the timer.\n\nOnce running:\nAll duplicate Start controls disable.\n\nEither attacking teammate may press End Turn.\n\nEnd Turn confirmation:\n\"Has your team completed all three time limits?\"\n\nNO:\nReturn.\n\nYES:\nSwitch attacking/defending roles.\n\nHigher team point total:\nWins.\n\nTie:\nPaired tiebreak possessions until separated.\n\n\n=================================================="
