    "engine": "ttt",
    "tournament": false,
    "tag": false,
    "rules": "==================================================\n\nSUPPORTED FORMAT:\n- 1v1 only\n\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nClaim mechanic tiles on a 3×3 board.\n\nFirst player to create:\n3 in a row\nwins.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nBOARD GENERATION\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nBrowser creates:\n3×3 board.\n\nEach of 9 tiles contains:\nOne random mechanic.\n\nRandomly choose:\n- Starting player.\n- Which player is X.\n- Which player is O.\n\nDisplay this clearly.\n\nExample:\n\nBRADLEY = X\nALEX = O\nBRADLEY STARTS\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nTURN ENFORCEMENT\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nPlayers will manage actual turn-taking themselves.\n\nBrowser does NOT need to hard-lock every tile based on whose turn it thinks it is.\n\nReason:\nThis reduces accidental deadlocks when players need to correct something.\n\nBrowser should still display:\n\"Starting Player: Bradley\"\n\nBut after that:\nPlayers are responsible for alternating fairly.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nSELECTING AN UNCLAIMED TILE\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nAny unclaimed mechanic tile is a button.\n\nWhen player selects it:\n\nPopup:\n\n\"DID YOU SUCCESSFULLY COMPLETE:\n[Mechanic]?\"\n\nYES\nNO\n\n\nNO:\nClose popup.\nTile remains unclaimed.\n\nYES:\nPlace that player's X or O marker on tile.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nMISCLICK RECOVERY\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nA player may click a tile containing THEIR OWN marker.\n\nPopup:\n\n\"REMOVE YOUR MARKER FROM THIS TILE?\nUse this only if the tile was marked by mistake.\"\n\nYES:\nRemove their marker.\nTile becomes unclaimed again.\n\nNO:\nReturn unchanged.\n\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nA player may NOT remove:\nOpponent's marker.\n\nDo not show Remove option for opponent-owned tiles.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nREROLLING UNCLAIMED TILES\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nPlayers may verbally agree to reroll an unclaimed mechanic.\n\nHost receives:\nREROLL UNCLAIMED TILE\n\nHost selects:\nOne currently unclaimed tile.\n\nConfirmation:\n\n\"Both players agreed to replace this mechanic?\"\n\nConfirm:\nGenerate a new mechanic for that tile.\n\nCancel:\nNo change.\n\nClaimed tiles:\nCannot be rerolled.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nWIN DETECTION\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nAfter every successful tile claim:\n\nAutomatically check all:\n- Rows\n- Columns\n- Diagonals\n\nIf 3 matching markers appear:\nImmediately show winner state.\n\nDo not require Host to manually identify line.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nDRAW\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nHost gets:\nDRAW\n\nDraw may be used when:\n\n- All 9 tiles are claimed without 3-in-a-row.\nOR\n- Players agree the remaining board is unwinnable.\n\nBecause players manage turns manually:\nDo not require the program to mathematically prove the board is unwinnable before allowing Host Draw.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nRESULT SAFETY\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nBefore reward:\n\nShow:\n\"[PLAYER] COMPLETED 3 IN A ROW\"\n\nAllow Host:\nCorrect Board\n\nCorrect Board returns to board before reward application.\n\nDo not destroy the board state immediately upon detecting the line.\n\n\n=================================================="
