    "rules": "==================================================\n\nSUPPORTED FORMATS:\n- 1v1\n- 1v1v1\n- 1v1v1v1\n- 2v2\n\n\nCORE OBJECTIVE\n\nUse ONE randomly selected mechanic and progressively score that same mechanic into increasingly precise target requirements.\n\nThe mechanic itself does NOT change between rungs.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nMECHANIC SELECTION\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nBrowser randomly selects:\n1 mechanic.\n\nThat mechanic is used by EVERY participant for the entire Challenge.\n\nDisplay it prominently at all times.\n\nExample:\n\nSELECTED MECHANIC:\nFLIP RESET\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nLADDER\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nRUNG 1:\nAny Valid Goal\n\nRUNG 2:\nTop-Half Goal\n\nRUNG 3:\nTop-Corner Goal\n\nRUNG 4:\nCrossbar-Down Goal\n\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nThe selected mechanic must still be completed on every rung.\n\nExample:\n\nIf selected mechanic is Flip Reset:\n\nRung 1:\nAny valid Flip Reset goal.\n\nRung 2:\nFlip Reset into top half.\n\nRung 3:\nFlip Reset into top corner.\n\nRung 4:\nFlip Reset crossbar-down.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nATTEMPTS\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nEach player gets:\n2 attempts PER RUNG.\n\nIf player succeeds on either attempt:\n- Mark rung completed.\n- Immediately advance player to next rung.\n- Unused attempt on completed rung is discarded.\n\nIf player fails BOTH attempts:\n- Their run ends.\n- Record highest rung successfully completed.\n\nDo NOT end a player's run after only one miss.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nRESULT MEASUREMENT\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nTrack:\nHIGHEST COMPLETED RUNG.\n\nExample:\n\nPlayer completed:\nAny Goal\nTop Half\n\nThen failed both Top Corner attempts.\n\nResult:\nCompleted Rung 2.\n\n\nCROSSBAR DOWN:\nFinal rung.\n\nCompleting Crossbar Down:\nFull ladder completion.\n\n\n==================================================\n1v1 — PRECISION LADDER\n==================================================\n\nBoth players use:\nSame mechanic.\n\nEach performs their ladder run.\n\nHigher completed rung:\nWins.\n\nIf both stop at same rung:\nDraw.\n\nIf both complete Crossbar Down:\nDraw.\n\nNo tiebreak is required.\n\n\nBROWSER UI\n\nShow full ladder visually:\n\n[1] ANY GOAL\n[2] TOP HALF\n[3] TOP CORNER\n[4] CROSSBAR DOWN\n\nFor each player show:\n- Current rung\n- Attempt 1 / 2\n- Completed rungs\n- Finished status\n\nSuggested controls for active player:\n\nMADE\nMISSED\n\nMADE:\n- Complete current rung.\n- Advance.\n\nMISSED:\n- Increment rung attempt.\n- First miss → allow second attempt.\n- Second miss → finish run.\n\nProvide:\nUNDO LAST INPUT\n\nHost also has:\nDRAW\n\nbecause equal progression is a valid final result.\n\n\n==================================================\n1v1v1 — PRECISION LADDER\n==================================================\n\nAll players:\nSame mechanic.\nSame ladder.\n2 attempts per rung.\n\nRank by:\nHighest completed rung.\n\nMultiple players may share placement.\n\nIMPORTANT FINAL-RUNG RULE:\n\nAny player who completes:\nCrossbar Down\n\nhas reached the maximum result.\n\nIf multiple players complete Crossbar Down:\nThey tie at the highest possible placement.\n\nDo NOT invent another rung to separate them.\n\n\nBROWSER\n\nIndependent ladder card per player.\n\nPlayers may perform runs in browser-randomized sequential order to simplify tracking.\n\nAfter all runs:\nAutomatically calculate placements.\n\nEqual rung:\nShared placement.\n\n\n==================================================\n1v1v1v1 — PRECISION LADDER\n==================================================\n\nSame structure with 4 players.\n\nFull placement based on highest completed rung.\n\nTies:\nShared placements.\n\nNo forced tiebreak.\n\n\n==================================================\n2v2 — PRECISION LADDER\n==================================================\n\nAll 4 players:\nSame mechanic.\nSame ladder.\n2 attempts per rung.\n\nEach player produces:\nOne individual ladder result.\n\nTEAM COMPARISON:\n\nStep 1:\nCompare each team's BEST individual result.\n\nWhichever team has the player who went farther:\nWins.\n\nExample:\n\nTeam A:\nA1 = Top Corner\nA2 = Top Half\n\nTeam B:\nB1 = Top Half\nB2 = Any Goal\n\nTeam A wins.\n\n\nSTEP 2 — BEST PLAYERS TIED\n\nIf each team's best player reached the same rung:\n\nCompare each team's SECOND player.\n\nExample:\n\nTeam A:\nA1 = Top Corner\nA2 = Top Half\n\nTeam B:\nB1 = Top Corner\nB2 = Any Goal\n\nTeam A wins because second-best result is farther.\n\n\nSTEP 3 — BOTH TEAM RESULTS IDENTICAL\n\nExample:\n\nTeam A:\nTop Corner / Top Half\n\nTeam B:\nTop Corner / Top Half\n\nResult:\nDRAW.\n\nDo not force additional ladder attempts.\n\n\nBROWSER\n\nAfter all 4 runs:\nSort each team's two results internally from highest → lowest.\n\nCompare:\nBest vs Best.\n\nIf tied:\nSecond vs Second.\n\nIf still tied:\nDraw.\n\nShow comparison visibly before result.\n\n\n=================================================="
