    "rules": "==================================================\n\nSUPPORTED FORMATS:\n- 1v1\n- 1v1v1\n- 1v1v1v1\n- 2v2\n\n\nTARGET:\nFirst individual to 3 points.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nLETTER GENERATION\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nBrowser generates:\nOne valid random letter.\n\nA \"valid letter\" should have at least one approved mechanic in the existing mechanic database.\n\nDo not deliberately generate letters with no possible mechanic.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nROUND RULE\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nOnce letter appears:\n\nPlayers may attempt ANY legitimate mechanic whose accepted name begins with that letter.\n\nExample:\nLetter M\nPossible:\nMusty Flick\n\nThe first player who successfully scores a valid mechanic beginning with that letter:\nEarns 1 point.\n\nThen:\nGenerate a new letter.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nREPEATED LETTER RULE\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nThe same letter MAY appear again later.\n\nIf it does:\nPlayers may NOT use a mechanic that has already been successfully used for that same letter earlier in this Challenge.\n\nExample:\n\nFirst M round:\nMusty Flick was winning mechanic.\n\nLater M:\nMusty Flick cannot be used again.\n\nPlayers manually enforce the actual mechanic-name history.\n\nBrowser does not need to validate mechanic names unless a mechanic-selection database UI is added later.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nREROLL\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nIf EVERYONE verbally agrees:\nHost may reroll current letter.\n\nHost button:\nREROLL LETTER\n\nNo hard limit.\n\nReroll:\nDoes not award a point.\nSimply replaces current letter.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n1v1\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nIndividual score:\n0–3.\n\nFirst player to 3:\nWins.\n\nBrowser may track points OR players may manually track.\n\nRecommended browser:\nHost has:\n+1 PLAYER A\n+1 PLAYER B\n\nAfter point:\nAutomatically generate next letter if desired.\n\nProvide:\nUNDO LAST POINT\n\nFirst to 3:\nWinner.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n1v1v1\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nEach player has individual point total.\n\nFirst player to reach 3:\nWins Challenge immediately.\n\nFor lower placement:\nRank remaining players by their current point totals at moment winner reaches 3.\n\nEqual totals:\nShared placement.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n1v1v1v1\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nSame with 4 players.\n\nFirst individual to 3:\n1st.\n\nOthers:\nRank by current scores.\nEqual scores share placement.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n2v2 — INDIVIDUAL WINNER WINS FOR TEAM\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nAll 4 players have INDIVIDUAL point totals.\n\nDo NOT combine teammate points.\n\nFirst individual to reach:\n3 points\n\nwins Challenge for their team.\n\nExample:\n\nA1 = 3\nA2 = 0\n\nB1 = 2\nB2 = 2\n\nTeam A wins because A1 individually reached the target.\n\nIf an ambiguous simultaneous finish occurs:\nHost may undo/retry that letter round or decide which valid mechanic clearly scored first.\n\nBrowser cannot detect Rocket League timing automatically.\n\n\n=================================================="
