    "engine": "airdribble",
    "tournament": false,
    "tag": false,
    "rules": "==================================================\n\nSUPPORTED FORMATS:\n- 1v1\n- 1v1v1\n- 1v1v1v1\n- 2v2\n- 1v2 / 2v1\n- 1v3 / 3v1\n\n\nCORE OBJECTIVE\n\nProduce the longest VALID continuous air dribble that ends in a goal.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nATTEMPTS\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nEach player receives:\n\n1 official attempt\n\nunless entering a tiebreak.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nVALID AIR-DRIBBLE TIMER START\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nTimer begins:\n\nAs soon as the player jumps off the wall or ground WITH the ball and begins the active air dribble.\n\nA non-active player manually starts the browser stopwatch at that moment.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nTIMER END\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nStop timer when ANY of the following occurs:\n\n1. Ball fully enters the goal.\n2. Ball touches ground.\n3. Player's car touches ground.\n4. Player clearly breaks the continuous-air-dribble rules.\n5. Attempt otherwise becomes invalid.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nSUCCESS REQUIREMENT\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nThe attempt must end in:\nA VALID GOAL.\n\nIf the air dribble lasts a long time but does not score:\nOfficial attempt time = 0.\n\nOnly successful scoring air dribbles receive their recorded elapsed time.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nCONTINUITY RULE\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nAir dribble must remain continuous.\n\nNot allowed:\n- Ending the aerial sequence.\n- Landing.\n- Turtle/reset setup on ground to get back up.\n- Restarting a second unrelated air dribble during same attempt.\n\n\nAllowed:\n- Flip resets.\n- Flicks.\n- Other airborne mechanics.\n\nThey are allowed only if all other Longest Air Dribble rules remain valid.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nWALL / CEILING RULE\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nA wall or ceiling touch does NOT automatically invalidate the attempt.\n\nHowever:\n\nIf player effectively lands on their wheels on the wall and re-establishes a grounded/wall-driving setup:\nAttempt ends.\n\nBrief contact that remains part of the continuous aerial motion may be accepted.\n\nPlayers judge mechanical validity themselves.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nBROWSER TURN ORDER\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nBrowser randomly chooses run order.\n\nOnly one player performs an official timed attempt at a time.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nTIMER OPERATOR\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nThe ACTIVE PLAYER may NOT operate their own timer.\n\nEvery other active player can see:\n\nSTART TIMER\n\nThe first eligible person to press Start becomes:\n\nTIMER OPERATOR\n\nfor that attempt.\n\nOnce locked:\nOnly that Timer Operator can normally press:\n\nSTOP TIMER\nREDO TIMER\nSUBMIT TIME\n\nHost always has emergency takeover controls.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nAFTER TIMER STOPS\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nTimer Operator chooses:\n\nVALID GOAL\nFAILED ATTEMPT\n\n\nVALID GOAL:\nRecorded stopwatch time becomes provisional.\n\nFAILED ATTEMPT:\nTime becomes 0.\n\n\nThen show:\n\nSUBMIT OFFICIAL RESULT\nREDO ATTEMPT TIMING\n\n\nREDO should be used for:\n- Incorrect start.\n- Incorrect stop.\n- Timing mishap.\n\nIf Redo is chosen:\nDiscard provisional time/result and run that player's official attempt again.\n\nOnce Submit is pressed:\nThat becomes the player's official normal attempt.\n\n\n==================================================\n1v1 — LONGEST AIR DRIBBLE\n==================================================\n\nEach:\n1 attempt.\n\nHigher valid time:\nWins.\n\nFailed attempt:\n0.\n\nTie:\nEach player receives 1 additional attempt.\n\nCompare the new tiebreak attempt times.\n\nRepeat until separated.\n\n\n==================================================\n1v1v1 — LONGEST AIR DRIBBLE\n==================================================\n\nEach player:\n1 attempt.\n\nRank valid times:\nLongest → shortest.\n\nFailed attempt:\n0.\n\nIf players tie:\nOnly tied players take one additional attempt.\n\nUse new tiebreak times to separate tied placement.\n\nRepeat as necessary.\n\n\n==================================================\n1v1v1v1 — LONGEST AIR DRIBBLE\n==================================================\n\nSame with 4 players.\n\nRank 1st–4th.\n\nOnly tied players redo tiebreak attempts.\n\n\n==================================================\n2v2 — INDIVIDUAL WINNER WINS FOR TEAM\n==================================================\n\nEach of 4 players:\n1 official attempt.\n\nDo NOT sum teammates' times.\n\nLongest INDIVIDUAL valid time:\nWins entire Challenge for that player's team.\n\nIf top times from DIFFERENT teams tie:\nOnly those tied players receive 1 extra attempt.\n\nRepeat until one team has the top individual result.\n\nIf the only highest-tied players are teammates:\nTheir team already wins.\nNo need to separate them.\n\n\n==================================================\n1v2 / 2v1 — 2× SOLO LONGEST AIR DRIBBLE\n==================================================\n\nEach participant:\n1 attempt.\n\nSolo Weighted Time:\n\nSolo Valid Time ×2\n\nDuo Score:\n\nDuo A Valid Time\n+\nDuo B Valid Time\n\nCompare:\nSolo weighted time\nvs\nDuo sum.\n\nHigher:\nWins.\n\nIf tied:\nAll 3 participants take one additional attempt.\n\nCompare only new tiebreak results:\n\nSolo tiebreak time ×2\nvs\nDuo A + Duo B.\n\nRepeat until separated.\n\n\n==================================================\n1v3 / 3v1 — 3× SOLO LONGEST AIR DRIBBLE\n==================================================\n\nEach:\n1 attempt.\n\nSolo:\nValid Time ×3\n\nTrio:\nA + B + C valid times.\n\nHigher:\nWins.\n\nTie:\nAll 4 players take one new tiebreak attempt.\n\nCompare:\nSolo ×3\nvs\nTrio sum.\n\nRepeat until separated.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nTIME DISPLAY\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nStore precise stopwatch value.\n\nDisplay at least:\n0.1 second precision.\n\nDo not round individual values before:\n- Multiplying Solo time\n- Adding team times\n\nUse full stored precision for calculation.\nRound only visual display.\n\n\n=================================================="
