    "tag": false,
    "rules": "==================================================\n\nSUPPORTED FORMATS:\n- 1v1\n- 2v2\n\n\nCORE OBJECTIVE\n\nSay valid, unused Rocket League car names to reverse a continuously moving bomb away from yourself and toward the opponent.\n\nUnlike Name a Car:\nThere are no discrete 10-second turns.\n\nThe bomb itself IS the timer.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nBOMB TRACK\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nUse horizontal track:\n\nPLAYER / TEAM A\n[LEFT ENDPOINT]\n\n---------- CENTER ----------\n\n[RIGHT ENDPOINT]\nPLAYER / TEAM B\n\n\nBomb starts:\nExactly at center.\n\nBrowser randomly chooses initial direction:\n\nToward A\nor\nToward B.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nBOMB SPEED\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nFrom exact center:\nBomb takes approximately:\n\n10.0 seconds\n\nto reach either endpoint if never reversed.\n\nUse constant speed.\n\nConceptual normalized coordinates:\n\nLeft endpoint = -1\nCenter = 0\nRight endpoint = +1\n\nSpeed magnitude:\n0.1 units / second\n\nTherefore:\nCenter → endpoint = 10 seconds.\nFull endpoint-to-endpoint distance = 20 seconds.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nVALID ANSWER ACTION\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nOnly the player/team the bomb is CURRENTLY MOVING TOWARD may reverse it.\n\nTargeted player:\n\n1. Says valid unused Rocket League car aloud.\n2. Presses:\n\nVALID ANSWER — REVERSE BOMB\n\n\nAt exact authoritative press timestamp:\n\n- Compute current bomb position.\n- Preserve that position.\n- Reverse velocity direction.\n\nThe bomb does NOT:\n- Reset to center.\n- Reset a timer.\n- Teleport.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nWHY TIMING MATTERS\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nIf player answers immediately:\nBomb reverses while still far away.\n\nIf player waits:\nBomb gets close to their endpoint before they reverse it.\n\nThen opponent has more distance/time before it reaches them.\n\nThis creates the tug-of-war timing strategy.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nUNUSED ANSWER RULE\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nCar name cannot have been said previously during that Bomb Tug Challenge.\n\nInvalid/duplicate answer:\nDoes NOT reverse bomb.\n\nPlayers enforce spoken validity.\n\nUse same central Car database for disputes.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n1v1 — CAR BOMB TUG\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nOne player on each endpoint.\n\nOnly currently targeted player gets active:\nREVERSE BOMB\n\nOpponent's button:\nDisabled.\n\nAfter valid reversal:\nControls immediately swap.\n\nIf bomb reaches endpoint:\nThat player loses.\nOpponent wins.\n\nNo tie.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n2v2 — CAR BOMB TUG\n==================================================\n\nOne bomb.\n\nTeam A:\n2 players.\n\nTeam B:\n2 players.\n\nIf bomb is moving toward Team A:\nBOTH Team A players may attempt to provide an answer.\n\nEither teammate can say a valid unused car and press Reverse.\n\nThe FIRST accepted valid Reverse input:\nChanges direction.\n\nImmediately after direction changes:\nBoth Team A Reverse buttons disable.\nBoth Team B buttons enable.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n2v2 DOUBLE-PRESS PROTECTION\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nThis must use an atomic direction-state/version check.\n\nExample:\n\nA1 and A2 both press Reverse 20 ms apart.\n\nA1's request reaches server first:\nAccepted.\nDirection changes toward Team B.\n\nA2's request was created under old \"bomb moving toward Team A\" state:\nReject as stale.\n\nDo NOT allow A2's late press to reverse the bomb immediately back toward Team A.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n2v2 WIN\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nIf bomb reaches Team A endpoint:\nTeam A loses.\n\nIf reaches Team B endpoint:\nTeam B loses.\n\nNo individual elimination.\n\n\n==================================================\nBOMB SYNCHRONIZATION\n==================================================\n\nDO NOT animate bomb by each client independently incrementing position every frame as authoritative state.\n\nStore authoritative state:\n\n- Current position at last direction change\n- Current direction\n- Last direction-change timestamp\n- Game started timestamp\n- Active/finished status\n- State version\n\nEach browser renders position based on:\nAuthoritative position + elapsed authoritative time.\n\nReconnect:\nReconstruct correct current position.\n\nA player refreshing must NOT reset bomb.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nBOMB ENDPOINT\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nWhen calculated bomb position reaches endpoint:\n\nAtomically mark Challenge:\nFINISHED.\n\nStop accepting Reverse events.\n\nPlay:\nExplosion animation/sound on losing side.\n\nShow winner.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nINVALID PRESS / CHEATING RECOVERY\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nIf a player presses Reverse after saying:\n- Duplicate car\n- Invalid car\n- No answer\n\nHost may immediately press:\n\nUNDO LAST REVERSE\n\n\nUndo must NOT simply flip current direction at the current moment.\n\nIt should reconstruct game as though invalid reversal NEVER OCCURRED.\n\nUse event history.\n\nExample:\n\nAt t=5.0:\nInvalid reversal happened.\n\nAt t=6.5:\nHost corrects it.\n\nRecompute bomb trajectory from t=5.0 as if it continued toward original target for those extra 1.5 seconds.\n\nIf that corrected trajectory means endpoint should already have been hit:\nApply the loss.\n\nThis prevents an invalid reversal from buying free time.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nDISPUTE MODE\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nHost can temporarily:\n\nPAUSE FOR DISPUTE\n\nThis freezes authoritative bomb state.\n\nResolve whether answer was valid.\n\nThen:\n- Keep reversal\nor\n- Undo reversal\n\nResume from corrected position.\n\nUse this only when needed.\n\n\n=================================================="
