    "rules": "==================================================\n\nSUPPORTED FORMATS:\n- 1v1\n- 2v2\n\nIMPORTANT:\nDo NOT include a 1v1v1v1 Multi-Ball Rush version in the final implementation pool.\n\nThis Challenge is meant to remain a straightforward simultaneous-ball race in formats that naturally support two opposing sides.\n\n\n==================================================\nCORE OBJECTIVE\n==================================================\n\nMultiple Rocket League balls are active at the same time.\n\nPlayers may attack whichever live ball they want.\n\nThe objective is NOT:\n- Possession time\n- Total shots\n- Fancy goals\n- Ball-specific scoring\n\nThe objective is simply:\n\nREACH 2 VALID GOALS BEFORE THE OPPONENT / OPPOSING TEAM.\n\n\nNormal gameplay is allowed:\n\n- Boost\n- Defense\n- Saves\n- Bumps\n- Demos\n- Rotations\n- Challenging either live ball\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nOWN-GOAL RULE\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nAn own goal does NOT give personal credit to the player who put the ball into their own net.\n\nFor team scoring:\nUse Rocket League's normal team goal result.\n\nFor individual scoring where applicable:\nOnly a legitimate attacking goal credited to that player's intended attacking side counts.\n\nDo not allow players to manufacture personal points by intentionally own-goaling.\n\n\n==================================================\n1v1 — MULTI-BALL RUSH\n==================================================\n\nBalls:\n2\n\nPlayers:\n1 vs 1\n\nBoth balls are live simultaneously.\n\nEach player may:\n- Attack either ball.\n- Switch between balls freely.\n- Defend either ball.\n\nTarget:\nFirst player to 2 valid goals.\n\nThe moment one player reaches:\n2\n\nthe Challenge ends immediately.\n\nNo match timer.\n\nNo normal tie state.\n\nIf two goals somehow occur essentially simultaneously and both would create a 2–2 final state:\nHost determines which scoring event clearly completed first.\n\nIf genuinely impossible to tell:\nRedo from the previous tied score state if practical, or replay a deciding goal race.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nBROWSER UI — 1v1\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nBecause Rocket League is not connected to browser:\n\nRecommended simple score tracker:\n\nPLAYER A\n0 / 2\n\nPLAYER B\n0 / 2\n\nHost controls:\n\n+ GOAL A\n+ GOAL B\n\nEach accepted goal:\nIncrement score.\n\nAt 2:\nFreeze goal buttons.\nShow winner.\n\nAlso provide:\n\nUNDO LAST GOAL\n\nThis should restore:\n- Previous score\n- Finished/not-finished state\n\nDo not require the browser to know which physical ball scored.\n\n\n==================================================\n2v2 — MULTI-BALL RUSH\n==================================================\n\nBalls:\n4\n\nPlayers:\n2 vs 2\n\nAll 4 balls are active.\n\nBoth teams may:\n- Attack any ball.\n- Defend any ball.\n- Split up.\n- Double-team one ball.\n- Rotate normally.\n\nTarget:\nFirst TEAM to 2 valid goals.\n\nTeam goals are collective.\n\nExample:\n\nA1 scores first goal.\nA2 scores second goal.\n\nTeam A reaches 2 and wins.\n\nA single player does not need to score both.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n2v2 BROWSER UI\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nTEAM A\n0 / 2\n\nTEAM B\n0 / 2\n\nHost:\n+ TEAM A GOAL\n+ TEAM B GOAL\n\nAt 2:\nAutomatic winner state.\n\nUNDO LAST GOAL:\nAvailable before reward confirmation.\n\n\n=================================================="
