    "engine": "manual",
    "tournament": true,
    "tag": true,
    "rules": "==================================================\n\nSUPPORTED FORMATS:\n- 1v1\n- 1v1v1\n- 1v1v1v1 Tournament\n- 1v2 / 2v1 Tag-Team\n- 1v3 / 3v1 Tag-Team\n\n\nCORE OBJECTIVE\n\nTwo opposing players create one combined shot requirement themselves.\n\nBrowser does NOT generate the mechanic.\n\nThe players simultaneously contribute one mechanic/mechanic-related requirement each.\n\nThose two requirements are combined.\n\nThen both players race to be:\nFIRST TO SCORE THE COMBINED SHOT.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nCALLING THE REQUIREMENTS\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nAt beginning of mini-match:\n\nPlayer A and Player B each say:\nONE mechanic OR mechanic-related requirement.\n\nThey should say them at essentially the same time to prevent one player from deliberately choosing a counter-requirement after hearing the other.\n\nExamples:\n\nA:\n\"Flip Reset\"\n\nB:\n\"Top Corner\"\n\nCombined requirement:\nFlip Reset into Top Corner.\n\n\nA:\n\"Musty Flick\"\n\nB:\n\"Crossbar Down\"\n\nCombined:\nMusty Flick Crossbar Down.\n\n\nA:\n\"Ceiling Shot\"\n\nB:\n\"Double Tap\"\n\nCombined:\nCeiling Shot + Double Tap sequence.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nWHAT COUNTS AS A REQUIREMENT\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nValid call can be:\n- Mechanic\n- Shot placement\n- Speed requirement\n- Bounce restriction\n- Setup requirement\n- Other clearly understandable mechanic-related condition\n\nBoth sides must understand the combined requirement before attempting it.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nUNREASONABLE COMBINATION\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nIf BOTH players agree:\n\n\"This combination is too hard / unrealistic\"\n\nDiscard it completely.\n\nBoth players make new simultaneous calls.\n\nThere is no penalty.\n\nNo limit on consensual redraw/re-call.\n\n\nIMPORTANT:\nOne player alone cannot force a reroll simply because they dislike the combination.\n\nBoth must agree.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nACTIVE PLAY\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nOnce requirement is agreed:\n\nBoth players may attempt it continuously.\n\nNo turn order.\n\nNo attempt limit.\n\nBoth play simultaneously in their own appropriate Rocket League setup / Free Play.\n\nFirst player to successfully SCORE the agreed combined shot:\nWins mini-match immediately.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nSIMULTANEOUS FINISH\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nIf both apparently score at almost the exact same time:\n\nPlayers/Host determine who clearly completed first.\n\nIf impossible to distinguish:\nCreate a new combined mechanic and replay a deciding race.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nBROWSER UI\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nBrowser does not need mechanic text input.\n\nKeep UI simple:\n\nMATCHUP:\nBradley vs Alex\n\nSTATUS:\nCREATE A COMBINED MECHANIC VERBALLY\n\nHost controls:\n\nSTART RACE\n\nThen:\n\nBRADLEY SCORED FIRST\nALEX SCORED FIRST\n\nAlso:\n\nRESTART COMBINED REQUIREMENT\n\nfor cases where both agree it was unreasonable after starting.\n\nNo browser attempt counter.\n\n\n==================================================\n1v1 — COMBINED MECHANIC\n==================================================\n\nOne combined-mechanic race.\n\nFirst valid scorer:\nWins.\n\nNo timer.\n\nNo draw.\n\n\n==================================================\n1v1v1 — THREE-PLAYER COMBINED MECHANIC\n==================================================\n\nAll 3 players simultaneously contribute:\nONE mechanic OR mechanic-related requirement each.\n\nCombine all 3 requirements into one shared shot.\n\nExample:\nPlayer A: Flip Reset\nPlayer B: Top Corner\nPlayer C: Crossbar Down\n\nCombined shot:\nFlip Reset + Top Corner + Crossbar Down.\n\nAll 3 players race simultaneously in their own setup / Free Play.\n\nNo timer.\nNo attempt limit.\n\nFirst player to successfully score a shot that satisfies ALL 3 requirements:\nWins.\n\nIf all 3 agree the combination is unreasonable or effectively impossible:\nDiscard it and make 3 fresh simultaneous calls.\n\nIf two or more players appear to finish at the same time and nobody can clearly determine who was first:\nCreate a fresh 3-part combined mechanic and replay the deciding race.\n\nBrowser:\nUse normal 3-player placement/result controls.\nThe first scorer is 1st.\nIf 2nd and 3rd need to be distinguished for placement, the remaining two players create a fresh normal 2-part Combined Mechanic and race for 2nd.\n\n\n==================================================\n1v1v1v1 — COMBINED MECHANIC TOURNAMENT\n==================================================\n\nUse Global Tournament System.\n\nEach semifinal pairing:\nCreates its OWN combined mechanic.\n\nThe two semifinals:\nRun simultaneously.\n\nDo not force both semifinal pairs to use same combination.\n\nAfter semis:\n\nFinal pair:\nCreates fresh combined mechanic.\n\n3rd-place pair:\nCreates fresh combined mechanic.\n\nHost chooses:\nSimultaneous\nor\nSequential.\n\nEach mini-match:\nFirst scorer wins.\n\n\n==================================================\n1v2 / 2v1 — TAG-TEAM COMBINED MECHANIC\n==================================================\n\nMini-Match 1:\nSolo vs Duo A.\n\nThose 2 players create one combined requirement.\n\nFirst scorer:\nWins mini-match.\n\n\nMini-Match 2:\nSolo vs Duo B.\n\nCreate a FRESH combined requirement.\n\nFirst scorer:\nWins mini-match.\n\n\nPossible result:\nSolo 2–0\nDuo 2–0\n1–1\n\n\nIf 1–1:\n\nBrowser randomly selects:\nDuo A or Duo B.\n\nSelected player faces Solo in:\nTIEBREAKER COMBINED MECHANIC.\n\nThey create a new combined requirement.\n\nFirst scorer:\nWins whole Challenge.\n\n\n==================================================\n1v3 / 3v1 — TAG-TEAM COMBINED MECHANIC\n==================================================\n\nMini-matches:\n\nSolo vs Trio A\nSolo vs Trio B\nSolo vs Trio C\n\nEach mini-match:\nFresh combined requirement.\n\nEach win:\n1 side point.\n\nFirst side to 2 mini-match wins:\nWins overall Challenge.\n\nBecause there are 3:\nNo overall tie.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nTAG-TEAM BROWSER\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nShow:\nMINI-MATCH 1 / 2\nor\n1 / 3\n\nCurrent pairing.\n\nSide score.\n\nFor 1v2:\nDo not randomize/reveal tiebreak player unless result reaches 1–1.\n\n\n=================================================="
