    "rules": "==================================================\n\nSUPPORTED FORMATS:\n- 1v1\n- 1v1v1\n- 1v1v1v1\n- 2v2\n- 1v2 / 2v1 Tag-Team\n- 1v3 / 3v1 Tag-Team\n\n\nCORE OBJECTIVE\n\nUse Rocket League's Knockout mode/settings.\n\nThe overall Challenge objective is:\nLAST PLAYER STANDING.\n\nBrowser does not simulate Knockout mechanics.\n\nPlayers play actual Rocket League Knockout.\n\nBrowser tracks:\n- Lives/eliminations\n- Placements\n- Browser-assigned teams\n- Tag-Team mini-duels\n\n\n==================================================\nSYMMETRIC LIFE RULE\n==================================================\n\nFor:\n\n1v1\n1v1v1\n1v1v1v1\n2v2\n\nEvery player gets:\n\n3 LIVES.\n\n\nFinal life lost:\nPlayer eliminated.\n\n\n==================================================\n1v1 — KNOCKOUT\n==================================================\n\nBoth:\n3 lives.\n\nContinue until one player reaches:\n0.\n\nSurvivor:\nWins.\n\nNo draw.\n\n\n==================================================\n1v1v1 — KNOCKOUT\n==================================================\n\nAll 3:\n3 lives.\n\nContinue until one survivor.\n\nPlacements:\nBased on elimination order.\n\nSimultaneous final-life eliminations:\nMay share placement if no clear order exists.\n\n\n==================================================\n1v1v1v1 — KNOCKOUT\n==================================================\n\nAll 4:\n3 lives.\n\nFFA.\n\nLast survivor:\n1st.\n\nOther placement:\nReverse elimination order.\n\nSame-time eliminations:\nShared placement where appropriate.\n\n\n==================================================\n2v2 — KNOCKOUT TEAM VERSION\n==================================================\n\nActual gameplay:\nFFA Knockout.\n\nBrowser randomly assigns:\nTwo players Team A.\nTwo players Team B.\n\nEach individual:\n3 lives.\n\nThe LAST surviving individual:\nWins Challenge for their browser team.\n\nIf remaining survivors are all from same team:\nThat team wins immediately.\n\nDo not make teammates continue fighting merely to determine which teammate personally survives longest.\n\n\n==================================================\nTAG-TEAM KNOCKOUT — ONE-LIFE RULE\n==================================================\n\nFor:\n1v2\n1v3\n\nEach mini-duel:\n1 life per player.\n\nFirst elimination:\nEnds mini-duel.\n\nDo not use normal 3-life Knockout for these Tag-Team segments.\n\n\n==================================================\n1v2 / 2v1 — TAG-TEAM KNOCKOUT\n==================================================\n\nMini-Duel 1:\nSolo vs Duo A.\n1 life each.\n\nMini-Duel 2:\nSolo vs Duo B.\n1 life each.\n\nEach mini-duel winner:\n+1 side win.\n\nIf:\n2–0\nor\n0–2\noverall winner is known.\n\nIf:\n1–1\n\nBrowser randomly selects:\nOne Duo member.\n\nTiebreak:\nSolo vs selected player.\n1 life each.\n\nWinner of tiebreak:\nWins whole Challenge.\n\n\n==================================================\n1v3 / 3v1 — TAG-TEAM KNOCKOUT\n==================================================\n\nSolo plays:\n\nTrio A\nTrio B\nTrio C\n\nOne mini-duel each.\n\nEach:\n1 life.\n\nFirst elimination:\nEnds duel.\n\nBest of 3:\nWins entire Challenge.\n\n\n==================================================\nKNOCKOUT / BULLET BALL COMMON ELIMINATION UI\n==================================================\n\nUse reusable Survival Challenge component.\n\nFor symmetric formats:\n\nEach player card shows:\n- Name\n- Browser team if applicable\n- Lives\n- Alive/Eliminated\n\nHost controls:\n-1 LIFE\n\nWhen life reaches 0:\nAutomatically mark Eliminated.\n\n\nFor players able to conveniently self-report:\nOptionally allow:\n\nI LOST A LIFE\n\non own screen.\n\nThis should open confirmation:\n\n\"Confirm you lost a life?\"\n\nDo NOT let normal players subtract lives from other players.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nELIMINATION ORDER\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nStore authoritative elimination event:\n\n- Player\n- Timestamp\n- Remaining lives before\n- Remaining lives after\n- Elimination rank if lives reached 0\n\nThis allows:\nUNDO LAST LIFE LOSS\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nUNDO\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nUndo must restore:\n\n- Life count\n- Alive status\n- Elimination order\n- Placement\n- Team-win state if match had ended\n\nIf Challenge already reached result screen:\nHost may still Correct Last Elimination before rewards.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nTEAM WIN DETECTION\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nFor 2v2:\n\nAfter every elimination:\nCheck surviving-team set.\n\nIf only Team A has living players:\nTeam A wins.\n\nIf only Team B:\nTeam B wins.\n\nDo not require exactly one total surviving player if all survivors are teammates.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nTAG-TEAM UI\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nShow:\n\nMINI-DUEL 1 / 2\nor\n1 / 3\n\nSOLO:\n[Name]\n\nOPPONENT:\n[Name]\n\nSIDE SCORE:\nSOLO 0\nTEAM 0\n\n\nAfter mini-duel:\nHost chooses:\n\nSOLO SURVIVED\nOPPONENT SURVIVED\n\nBrowser increments side score.\n\nFor 1v2:\nIf 1–1:\nOnly then generate/reveal random tiebreak opponent.\n\nFor 1v3:\nAfter one side reaches 2 wins:\nOverall winner may be declared immediately.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nTECHNICAL RESTART\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nIf Rocket League Knockout/Bullet Ball lobby fails before meaningful gameplay:\n\nHost:\nRESTART CURRENT MINI-DUEL\nor\nRESTART CHALLENGE\n\nFor Tag-Team:\nRestart Current Mini-Duel should NOT erase completed prior mini-duels.\n\nFor symmetric FFA:\nRestart Challenge clears all lives/elimination state."
