    "rules": "==================================================\n\nSUPPORTED FORMAT:\n- 1v1v1v1 only\n\n\nIMPORTANT CONCEPT\n\nThis Challenge uses an actual:\n\n2v2 Rocket League match\n\nbut the Battle is scored:\n\nINDIVIDUALLY.\n\nThe team result does NOT determine Board Game placement.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nTEAM GENERATION\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nBrowser randomly splits 4 players into:\n\nTEAM A\nTEAM B\n\nDisplay teams normally.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nMATCH LENGTH\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n3 minutes.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nROCKET LEAGUE GAMEPLAY\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nPlay normal 2v2.\n\nPlayers SHOULD cooperate with their teammate normally because they still need opportunities to score.\n\nHowever:\n\nEvery goal is credited to the individual player who scored it.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nINDIVIDUAL SCORING\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nEach player's Battle Score:\n\nNumber of individual Rocket League goals they personally scored.\n\n\nExample:\n\nTEAM A:\nA1 = 3 goals\nA2 = 0 goals\n\nTEAM B:\nB1 = 2 goals\nB2 = 1 goal\n\n\nIndividual placements:\n\n1st:\nA1 — 3\n\n2nd:\nB1 — 2\n\n3rd:\nB2 — 1\n\n4th:\nA2 — 0\n\n\nThe fact A1/A2 were teammates does not merge their scores.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nTIES\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nEqual individual goal totals:\nRemain tied.\n\nThere is NO overtime for individual-placement ties.\n\n\nExample:\n\nA1 = 2\nA2 = 1\nB1 = 2\nB2 = 0\n\nPlacements:\n\nA1 and B1:\nTied 1st\n\nA2:\n3rd\n\nB2:\n4th\n\n\nUse shared-placement reward logic as defined globally.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nTEAM MATCH SCORE\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nThe actual Rocket League team score does NOT determine Challenge winner.\n\nExample:\n\nTeam A wins Rocket League 4–3.\n\nBut:\nA1 = 4\nA2 = 0\nB1 = 2\nB2 = 1\n\nA1 still ranks 1st individually.\n\nDo not add a separate Team A Battle victory.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nBROWSER UI\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nBefore match:\n\nTEAM A:\nA1\nA2\n\nTEAM B:\nB1\nB2\n\n\nAfter match:\n\nHost enters individual goals:\n\nA1: [number]\nA2: [number]\nB1: [number]\nB2: [number]\n\n\nWhole numbers only.\nMinimum 0.\n\n\nBrowser automatically:\n- Sorts goal totals\n- Generates placements\n- Preserves ties\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nVALIDATION\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nOptional useful consistency check:\n\nSum of all individual goals should normally equal total non-own-goal scoring events.\n\nHowever:\nDo NOT block submission if Rocket League credited an unusual own goal or players manually agree on the correct values.\n\nHost can override.\n\nThe browser should prioritize the manually confirmed individual goal totals.\n\n\n=================================================="
