    "tag": false,
    "rules": "==================================================\n\nSUPPORTED FORMATS:\n- 1v2 / 2v1\n- 1v3 / 3v1\n\n\nROLES\n\nSOLO:\nSHARK\n\nTEAM:\nRUNNERS\n\n\n==================================================\nCORE OBJECTIVE\n==================================================\n\nThe Runner team must repeatedly cross from one Rocket League goal/end to the opposite goal/end while avoiding the Shark.\n\nThe Shark attempts to eliminate every Runner through demos/contact.\n\n\n==================================================\nROCKET LEAGUE SETTINGS\n==================================================\n\nEnable:\n\nDEMOLISH ON CONTACT\n\nUse the minimum practical demolition respawn time available in the agreed settings.\n\nTarget:\napproximately 1 second where available.\n\n\nRUNNERS:\nNO BOOST.\n\nSHARK:\nMay use boost normally.\n\n\n==================================================\nSTARTING POSITION\n==================================================\n\nAll active Runners begin:\n\nINSIDE / AT ONE GOAL END.\n\n\nShark begins:\nAway from that starting goal, positioned so the crossing can begin fairly.\n\nRecommended:\naround midfield.\n\n\nBrowser randomly chooses which goal/end is the initial Runner starting side if needed.\n\n\n==================================================\nCROSSING\n==================================================\n\nA Runner completes a crossing when they successfully travel from the current starting goal/end to the opposite goal/end without being eliminated.\n\n\nA Runner who reaches destination:\nIs SAFE for the remainder of that crossing.\n\n\nThe Shark continues hunting any Runner who has NOT yet reached safety.\n\n\nA crossing is complete once every currently surviving Runner has either:\n\n- Reached the destination safely\nOR\n- Been eliminated.\n\n\nThen:\nAll surviving Runners regroup at the destination goal.\n\nThat goal becomes the starting side for the next crossing.\n\nDirection therefore alternates back and forth.\n\n\n==================================================\nRUNNER ELIMINATION\n==================================================\n\nIf a Runner is demolished/contact-eliminated:\n\nThey are OUT for the ENTIRE Challenge.\n\nAfter respawning:\nThey must park/remain out of play.\n\nThey may not:\n- Block Shark\n- Protect teammates\n- Interfere with crossings\n\n\n==================================================\nSHARK DEMOS\n==================================================\n\nOnly Runner eliminations matter to Challenge state.\n\nIf the Shark gets demolished:\nShark simply respawns and continues.\n\nThe Shark is never permanently eliminated.\n\n\n==================================================\n1v2 — SHARK\n==================================================\n\nSolo:\nShark.\n\nDuo:\n2 Runners.\n\n\nRequired crossings:\n\n3.\n\n\nDUO WINS:\n\nAfter the third crossing is fully completed,\nat least ONE Runner is still alive.\n\n\nSHARK WINS:\n\nBoth Runners are eliminated before the team survives through all 3 required crossings.\n\n\nIf only one Runner remains:\nThat player continues subsequent crossings alone.\n\n\n==================================================\n1v3 — SHARK\n==================================================\n\nSolo:\nShark.\n\nTrio:\n3 Runners.\n\n\nRequired crossings:\n\n5.\n\n\nTRIO WINS:\n\nAfter completing Crossing #5,\nat least one Runner remains alive.\n\n\nSHARK WINS:\n\nAll 3 Runners are eliminated before completion of all 5 crossings.\n\n\n==================================================\nBROWSER UI\n==================================================\n\nDisplay:\n\nSHARK:\n[Player]\n\n\nRUNNERS:\n\nA — ALIVE\nB — ALIVE\nC — ALIVE\n\n\nCROSSING:\n\n2 / 5\n\n\nCURRENT DIRECTION:\n\nBLUE GOAL\n→\nORANGE GOAL\n\n\nFor each active Runner:\n\nSAFE THIS CROSSING\nor\nSTILL CROSSING\n\n\n==================================================\nRUNNER SELF-REPORT\n==================================================\n\nEach active Runner may have:\n\nI REACHED SAFETY\n\n\nThis marks them:\nSAFE for current crossing.\n\n\nHost also has:\n\nMARK RUNNER SAFE\n\nfor correction.\n\n\n==================================================\nDEMO INPUT\n==================================================\n\nHost:\n\nELIMINATE RUNNER\n\n\nOptional:\nRunner may self-report:\n\nI WAS DEMOED\n\n\nConfirmation required.\n\n\n==================================================\nADVANCING CROSSING\n==================================================\n\nBrowser automatically checks:\n\nFor every surviving Runner:\nAre they Safe?\n\nIf yes:\n\nCROSSING COMPLETE.\n\n\nIncrement:\nCrossing number.\n\nFlip direction.\n\nReset Safe state for surviving Runners.\n\nShow short:\n\n\"REGROUP AT OPPOSITE GOAL\"\n\nscreen.\n\nThen Host:\nSTART NEXT CROSSING\n\n\nDo not automatically begin before players reposition.\n\n\n==================================================\nSHARK EARLY WIN\n==================================================\n\nIf living Runner count becomes:\n\n0\n\nimmediately show:\nSHARK WINS.\n\nNo need to complete remaining crossings.\n\n\n==================================================\nRUNNER TEAM WIN\n==================================================\n\nAfter final required crossing completes:\n\nIf living Runner count >= 1:\n\nRUNNERS WIN.\n\n\n==================================================\nUNDO\n==================================================\n\nHost:\nUNDO LAST SHARK ACTION\n\nMust correctly restore:\n- Runner life state\n- Safe state\n- Crossing count/direction if necessary\n- Challenge result\n\n\n=================================================="
