    "engine": "boss",
    "tournament": false,
    "tag": false,
    "rules": "==================================================\n\nSUPPORTED FORMATS:\n- 1v2 / 2v1\n- 1v3 / 3v1\n\n\nROLES\n\nSOLO:\nBOSS\n\nDUO / TRIO:\nCHALLENGER TEAM\n\n\nBrowser randomly assigns:\n- Boss\n- Team\n\n\n==================================================\nOBJECTIVE\n==================================================\n\nEach round:\n\n1. Browser secretly gives the Boss 3 random mechanics.\n2. Boss chooses 1 of the 3.\n3. Selected mechanic is revealed to everyone.\n4. Team chooses one eligible teammate.\n5. That teammate gets 2 attempts.\n6. Success = survives that round.\n7. Failure on both attempts = permanently eliminated.\n\nThe Boss tries to eliminate the entire team before the required number of rounds is completed.\n\n\n==================================================\nROUND COUNTS\n==================================================\n\n1v2:\n4 ROUNDS\n\n1v3:\n6 ROUNDS\n\n\n==================================================\nMECHANIC DRAW\n==================================================\n\nAt beginning of every round:\n\nGenerate exactly:\n\n3 DISTINCT mechanics.\n\n\nWithin that single set of 3:\nNo duplicate.\n\nExample:\nDo not generate:\n\nMusty Flick\nMusty Flick\nDouble Tap\n\n\nHowever:\n\nMECHANICS MAY REPEAT IN LATER ROUNDS.\n\nThere is NO temporary discard pile.\n\nExample:\n\nRound 1 may contain:\nMusty Flick\n\nRound 4 may randomly contain:\nMusty Flick again.\n\nThat is valid.\n\n\nEvery round is an independent random draw.\n\n\n==================================================\nBOSS-ONLY MECHANIC VIEW\n==================================================\n\nBefore the Boss chooses:\n\nONLY the Boss sees:\n\nOPTION 1\n[Mechanic]\n\nOPTION 2\n[Mechanic]\n\nOPTION 3\n[Mechanic]\n\n\nEveryone else sees:\n\n\"THE BOSS IS CHOOSING A MECHANIC...\"\n\n\nThe Host must not receive an administrative view exposing the cards if the Host is a Team player.\n\n\n==================================================\nBOSS SELECTION\n==================================================\n\nBoss selects:\n\nONE of the 3 mechanics.\n\nConfirmation:\n\n\"Choose [Mechanic] for Round X?\"\n\nCONFIRM\nBACK\n\n\nOnce confirmed:\n\nReveal selected mechanic to EVERYONE.\n\n\nThe two unused mechanics disappear.\n\nThey are not placed into a discard pile.\n\n\n==================================================\nNO NORMAL REROLL\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT add a casual reroll button.\n\nThe Boss's power is choosing among the random 3.\n\nAllowing repeated rerolls would undermine the game.\n\nA technical restart of the round may exist through Host recovery, but should require explicit confirmation.\n\n\n==================================================\nTEAM CHALLENGER SELECTION\n==================================================\n\nOnce mechanic is revealed:\n\nThe Team verbally decides which eligible surviving player will attempt it.\n\n\nEligible players are shown as buttons.\n\nExample:\n\nCHOOSE CHALLENGER:\n\nALEX\nCHRIS\n\n\nA team member may submit the team's agreed choice.\n\nFirst confirmed selection locks it.\n\n\n==================================================\nCONSECUTIVE-PLAYER RULE\n==================================================\n\nA surviving Team player may NOT attempt two rounds in a row if another surviving teammate is available.\n\n\nExample:\n\nDuo:\nRound 1 = Alex\n\nIf both Alex and Chris remain alive:\nRound 2 MUST be Chris.\n\n\nFor Trio:\n\nRound 1 = Alex.\n\nIf Chris and Daniel are still alive:\nRound 2 must be Chris OR Daniel.\n\nAlex cannot be selected again immediately.\n\n\n==================================================\nONLY ONE SURVIVOR EXCEPTION\n==================================================\n\nIf only one Team member remains alive:\n\nIGNORE the consecutive-player rule.\n\nThat sole survivor may attempt every remaining round.\n\nThis is necessary to prevent a dead end.\n\n\n==================================================\nELIMINATED PLAYER\n==================================================\n\nA permanently eliminated player:\n\n- Cannot be selected.\n- Cannot attempt future mechanics.\n- Remains visually marked ELIMINATED.\n\nTheir elimination lasts the remainder of Boss Battle.\n\n\n==================================================\nATTEMPT FLOW\n==================================================\n\nSelected challenger gets:\n\n2 ATTEMPTS.\n\n\nATTEMPT 1:\n\nMADE\nMISSED\n\n\nIf MADE:\n\nPlayer survives.\n\nRound ends immediately.\n\nNo second attempt needed.\n\n\nIf MISSED:\n\nProceed to:\n\nATTEMPT 2.\n\n\nIf Attempt 2 MADE:\n\nPlayer survives.\n\n\nIf Attempt 2 MISSED:\n\nPlayer is ELIMINATED.\n\n\n==================================================\nNEXT ROUND\n==================================================\n\nIf at least one Team player remains:\n\nAdvance to next round.\n\nGenerate a fresh random set of 3 mechanics.\n\nBoss chooses again.\n\n\n==================================================\nBOSS EARLY WIN\n==================================================\n\nIf all Team players become eliminated at ANY point:\n\nBOSS WINS IMMEDIATELY.\n\nDo not continue unused rounds.\n\n\n==================================================\nTEAM WIN\n==================================================\n\nIf Team reaches the end of the required final round with:\n\nAT LEAST ONE PLAYER STILL ALIVE\n\nthe Team wins.\n\n\n1v2:\n\nSurvive through Round 4.\n\n\n1v3:\n\nSurvive through Round 6.\n\n\n==================================================\nTEAM RESULT\n==================================================\n\nIf Team wins:\nThe Duo/Trio is the winning Battle side.\n\nEven teammates eliminated during Boss Battle remain part of that winning team for normal team-result/reward handling.\n\nTheir elimination is only an internal Boss Battle mechanic.\n\n\n==================================================\nBROWSER UI\n==================================================\n\nPersistent display:\n\nBOSS:\n[Name]\n\nROUND:\n3 / 6\n\n\nTEAM:\n\nALEX\nALIVE\n\nCHRIS\nELIMINATED\n\nDANIEL\nALIVE\n\n\nCURRENT PHASE:\n\nBOSS CHOOSING\n\nor\n\nTEAM CHOOSING CHALLENGER\n\nor\n\nDANIEL — ATTEMPT 1 / 2\n\n\nCURRENT MECHANIC:\n\n[Mechanic]\n\n\n==================================================\nROUND HISTORY\n==================================================\n\nKeep a compact log:\n\nROUND 1\nBoss selected: Flip Reset\nChallenger: Alex\nResult: Survived on Attempt 2\n\nROUND 2\nSelected: Double Tap\nChallenger: Chris\nResult: Eliminated\n\n\nThis helps prevent confusion.\n\n\n==================================================\nUNDO / RECOVERY\n==================================================\n\nBefore next round's mechanic pool is generated:\n\nHost may:\n\nUNDO LAST ATTEMPT RESULT\n\n\nThis can restore:\n- Attempt count\n- Player survival\n- Round state\n\n\nIf a previous player was accidentally eliminated:\nRestore them.\n\n\n==================================================\nRECOVERY AFTER FUTURE RANDOM INFO EXISTS\n==================================================\n\nSuppose:\n\nRound 2 finished.\n\nRound 3's 3 mechanics have already been shown to Boss.\n\nThen Host realizes Round 2 result was entered incorrectly.\n\n\nDo NOT simply roll backward while keeping revealed Round 3 information.\n\nThat would leak future randomness.\n\n\nInstead:\n\nCORRECT PREVIOUS ROUND\n\nmust:\n\n1. Restore Round 2 to the appropriate state.\n2. Discard Round 3's already-generated mechanic pool.\n3. Clear any Round 3 selections.\n4. Once Round 2 finishes correctly, generate a NEW Round 3 pool.\n\n\nThis prevents players from gaining knowledge of future mechanic options through an undo.\n\n\n=================================================="
