    "rules": "==================================================\n\nSUPPORTED FORMAT:\n- 1v1v1v1 only\n\n\nDISPLAY NAME:\n\nROCKET LEAGUE OLYMPICS TOURNAMENT\n\n\nIMPORTANT:\nThis is NOT the multi-event 4-player Rocket Olympics from Game 32.\n\nGame 32:\nAll four compete across three events and earn Olympic points.\n\nTHIS game:\nUses a 4-player TOURNAMENT BRACKET.\n\nEvery bracket matchup is one randomly selected Sprint event.\n\n\n==================================================\nCURATED EVENT POOL\n==================================================\n\nEvery matchup independently draws from exactly these 5:\n\n1. SPEED SPRINT\n2. FREESTYLE SPRINT\n3. CROSSBAR SPRINT\n4. PINCH SPRINT\n5. KPH GUESS SPRINT\n\n\nUse the 1v1 Sprint rules already defined under Game 32.\n\n\n==================================================\nDUPLICATES ARE ALLOWED\n==================================================\n\nSelections are WITH REPLACEMENT.\n\nDo NOT use a temporary event discard pile.\n\n\nExample valid tournament:\n\nSemifinal A:\nSpeed Sprint\n\nSemifinal B:\nSpeed Sprint\n\nFinal:\nPinch Sprint\n\n3rd Place:\nSpeed Sprint\n\n\nThat is completely valid.\n\n\nThe unpredictability is intentional.\n\n\n==================================================\nBRACKET\n==================================================\n\nBrowser randomly creates:\n\nSEMIFINAL A\nPlayer A vs Player B\n\nSEMIFINAL B\nPlayer C vs Player D\n\n\nDo not allow manual reseeding after gameplay begins.\n\n\n==================================================\nSEMIFINAL EVENT REVEAL\n==================================================\n\nAt tournament start:\n\nRandomly choose:\n1 Sprint event for Semifinal A.\n\nRandomly choose:\n1 Sprint event for Semifinal B.\n\n\nReveal BOTH semifinal games.\n\nDo NOT generate/reveal the Final or 3rd-place games yet.\n\n\n==================================================\nSEMIFINALS ARE ALWAYS SIMULTANEOUS\n==================================================\n\nBoth semifinal cards become active at the same time.\n\nExample:\n\nSEMIFINAL A\nBradley vs Alex\nSPEED SPRINT\n\nSEMIFINAL B\nChris vs Daniel\nKPH GUESS SPRINT\n\n\nEach semifinal has:\n- Own game state\n- Own controls\n- Own result\n- Own timers/input state if required\n\n\nOne semifinal may finish before the other.\n\nDo not advance bracket until BOTH results are locked.\n\n\n==================================================\nSPRINT RULES\n==================================================\n\nSPEED SPRINT:\n- 1 shot each.\n- Successful goal KPH.\n- Higher wins.\n- Tie → repeat one each until separated.\n\nFREESTYLE SPRINT:\n- 2 attempts each.\n- Best successful shot wins.\n- If both miss or are judged tied, repeat until winner.\n\nCROSSBAR SPRINT:\n- 2 attempts each.\n- Most hits wins.\n- Tie → 1 additional attempt each until separated.\n\nPINCH SPRINT:\n- 1 pinch attempt each.\n- Fastest successful pinch goal wins.\n- Both miss / equal → repeat.\n\nKPH GUESS SPRINT:\n- A shoots, B guesses.\n- B shoots, A guesses.\n- Lower absolute error wins.\n- Tie → repeat paired sequence.\n\n\nEvery Sprint matchup MUST produce a winner.\n\n\n==================================================\nAFTER BOTH SEMIFINALS\n==================================================\n\nSemifinal winners:\n\n→ FINAL\nfor 1st / 2nd.\n\n\nSemifinal losers:\n\n→ 3RD-PLACE MATCH\nfor 3rd / 4th.\n\n\nOnly NOW:\n\nRandomly generate:\n- Final Sprint event\n- 3rd-place Sprint event\n\n\nReveal both.\n\n\nAgain:\nDuplicates are allowed.\n\n\n==================================================\nFINAL / 3RD-PLACE HOST CHOICE\n==================================================\n\nHost gets:\n\nPLAY BOTH SIMULTANEOUSLY\n\nor\n\nPLAY SEQUENTIALLY\n\n\n==================================================\nSIMULTANEOUS\n==================================================\n\nBoth match cards active.\n\nIndependent game states.\n\nPlayers complete both at same time.\n\n\n==================================================\nSEQUENTIAL\n==================================================\n\nHost chooses:\n\nPLAY FINAL FIRST\n\nor\n\nPLAY 3RD-PLACE FIRST\n\n\nChosen match becomes ACTIVE.\n\nOther displays:\n\nWAITING / UP NEXT\n\n\nAfter active match finishes:\nActivate second.\n\n\n==================================================\nPLACEMENTS\n==================================================\n\nFinal winner:\n1st\n\nFinal loser:\n2nd\n\n3rd-place winner:\n3rd\n\n3rd-place loser:\n4th\n\n\n==================================================\nMATCH RESULT CORRECTION\n==================================================\n\nHost may:\n\nUNDO MATCH RESULT\n\n\nCorrecting a semifinal:\n- Reopens only that semifinal.\n- Does not reshuffle bracket.\n\n\nIf Final/3rd event assignments have already been generated:\nKEEP those event assignments attached to their bracket slots.\n\nDo NOT reroll them merely because a semifinal result was corrected.\n\nThis prevents using a correction to fish for a more favorable Final event.\n\n\n=================================================="
