    "rules": "==================================================\n\nSUPPORTED FORMAT:\n- 1v1v1v1 only\n\n\nDISPLAY NAME:\n\n1v1 CHALLENGE ROULETTE TOURNAMENT\n\n\nCORE IDEA:\n\nA 4-player tournament where every individual matchup randomly becomes one of the existing Challenges specifically designed/named as a 1v1 game.\n\n\n==================================================\nIMPORTANT POOL RULE\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT include every Challenge that happens to support two players.\n\nOnly use the explicit approved \"1v1-style match\" pool below.\n\n\nUse stable Challenge IDs.\n\nDo NOT dynamically determine eligibility by searching the display string for \"1v1.\"\n\nThe explicit list is safer.\n\n\n==================================================\nAPPROVED ROULETTE POOL\n==================================================\n\n1. Normal 1v1\n\n2. Reverse 1v1\n\n3. Random Car 1v1\n\n4. Random Game Mode 1v1\n\n5. Turtle Unlimited Boost 1v1\n\n6. Red Light / Yellow Light / Green Light 1v1\n\n7. Heatseeker 1v1\n\n8. Random Official Arena / Random Custom Map 1v1\n\n9. No Boost 1v1\n\n10. Unlimited Boost 1v1\n\n11. Multi-Ball Rush 1v1\n\n12. Boomer Ball 1v1\n\n13. Lowest FOV 1v1\n\n14. Standing Up 1v1\n\n15. Combined Mechanic 1v1\n\n16. No Air Roll 1v1\n\n17. Rumble 1v1\n\n18. Dropshot 1v1\n\n19. Hoops 1v1\n\n20. Snow Day 1v1\n\n\n==================================================\nDO NOT INCLUDE\n==================================================\n\nExamples that should NOT be pulled into this Roulette:\n\n- Beat the Defender\n- Freestyle Shootout\n- HORSE\n- Mechanic Draft\n- Triathlon\n- Mechanic Gauntlet\n- Push Your Luck\n- Bullet Ball\n- Knockout\n- Secret Target Duel\n- Speed Ladder\netc.\n\nEven though some have a 1v1 format, they are not part of the explicitly approved \"1v1 game\" Roulette pool.\n\n\n==================================================\nNO RECURSION\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT include:\n\n- This Challenge Roulette Tournament itself\n- Rocket League Olympics Tournament\n- Player-Chosen Game Mode Tournament\n\nin its own random pool.\n\n\n==================================================\nDRAW METHOD\n==================================================\n\nEvery bracket matchup independently draws:\n\n1 Challenge\n\nfrom the approved pool.\n\n\nSelections are:\n\nWITH REPLACEMENT.\n\n\nDuplicates are allowed.\n\n\nExample:\n\nSemifinal A:\nNo Boost 1v1\n\nSemifinal B:\nNo Boost 1v1\n\nFinal:\nNo Boost 1v1\n\nThis is valid.\n\n\nThere is NO tournament-level discard pile.\n\n\n==================================================\nBRACKET\n==================================================\n\nRandomly generate 2 semifinals.\n\nReveal:\n\n- Players\n- Random Challenge selected for each semifinal\n\n\nDo NOT reveal/generate later-stage Challenges yet.\n\n\n==================================================\nSEMIFINALS\n==================================================\n\nALWAYS SIMULTANEOUS.\n\n\nEach selected Challenge uses its EXACT base 1v1 rules from its main Game definition.\n\n\nExamples:\n\nIf:\nNO BOOST 1v1\n\nUse Game 45 1v1 rules.\n\n\nIf:\nMULTI-BALL RUSH 1v1\n\nUse Game 51 1v1 rules.\n\n\nIf:\nRED LIGHT 1v1\n\nCreate an independent Red-Light engine for that semifinal.\n\n\n==================================================\nTWO SAME GAMES SIMULTANEOUSLY\n==================================================\n\nIf both semifinals draw the same Challenge:\n\nThey are still separate instances.\n\nExample:\n\nBoth draw Red Light.\n\nSemifinal A has:\nIts own random light sequence.\n\nSemifinal B has:\nIts own random light sequence.\n\n\nDo NOT share:\n- Timer\n- Light state\n- Random car\n- Arena\n- Game mode\n- Other subgame state\n\nbetween matchups.\n\n\n==================================================\nAFTER SEMIFINALS\n==================================================\n\nAfter BOTH results:\n\nCreate:\n\nFINAL\n\n3RD-PLACE MATCH\n\n\nThen independently draw:\n- Final Challenge\n- 3rd-place Challenge\n\n\nReveal them only now.\n\n\n==================================================\nFINAL / 3RD-PLACE\n==================================================\n\nHost chooses:\n\nSIMULTANEOUS\n\nor\n\nSEQUENTIAL\n\n\nSame tournament behavior as Global Tournament System.\n\n\n==================================================\nBASE CHALLENGE TIE RULES\n==================================================\n\nEvery matchup must resolve using the selected 1v1 Challenge's own tiebreak/OT logic.\n\nThe tournament wrapper does NOT add its own arbitrary tiebreak.\n\nExample:\n\nNormal 1v1:\nNext goal.\n\nMulti-Ball Rush:\nUse Multi-Ball Rush's deciding logic.\n\nCombined Mechanic:\nFirst valid combined shot.\n\n\nOnly submit bracket winner once the chosen Challenge itself has resolved.\n\n\n==================================================\nRANDOM GAME MODE NESTING\n==================================================\n\nIf Roulette selects:\n\nRANDOM GAME MODE 1v1\n\nthen Game 19 still performs its normal internal random mode selection.\n\nThis is allowed.\n\nThe tournament selected:\n\"Random Game Mode 1v1\"\n\nand that Challenge then independently selects its Rocket League mode.\n\n\n==================================================\nCORRECTION SAFETY\n==================================================\n\nMatch result correction:\nMust not reroll that match's selected Challenge.\n\nIf Host accidentally marks wrong semifinal winner:\n\nUNDO RESULT\n\nreopens same:\n- Players\n- Challenge\n- Subgame state if practical\n\n\nDo NOT use correction as a reroll button.\n\n\nIf later-stage Challenges have already been generated:\nKeep those Challenge assignments attached to their bracket slots.\n\n\n=================================================="
