    "rules": "==================================================\n\nSUPPORTED FORMAT:\n- 1v1v1v1 only\n\n\nRECOMMENDED DISPLAY NAME:\n\nRANDOM GAME MODE TOURNAMENT\n(Player-Chosen)\n\nINTERNAL ID:\n\nplayer_chosen_game_mode_tournament\n\n\nIMPORTANT:\nThis is NOT Game 19.\n\nGame 19:\nThe BROWSER randomly selects an approved Rocket League game mode.\n\nTHIS Challenge:\nTHE PLAYERS handle the game-mode choice/randomization themselves.\n\nThe browser does NOT select the mode.\n\n\n==================================================\nBROWSER RESPONSIBILITY\n==================================================\n\nBrowser only handles:\n\n- Random bracket\n- Matchups\n- Tournament progression\n- Simultaneous/sequential state\n- Winner/loser input\n- Final placements\n\n\nBrowser does NOT:\n\n- Choose game mode\n- Validate game mode\n- Store game mode\n- Randomize game mode\n- Require game-mode text input\n- Configure Rocket League\n\n\n==================================================\nPLAYER RESPONSIBILITY\n==================================================\n\nFor each mini-match:\n\nThe participating players decide among themselves what Rocket League mode they will play.\n\nThey may:\n- Randomize it themselves\n- Mutually choose it\n- Use another method they agree on\n\nThe browser does not care how they decide.\n\n\n==================================================\nBRACKET\n==================================================\n\nBrowser randomly creates:\n\nSEMIFINAL A\n\nSEMIFINAL B\n\n\nSemifinals are always:\n\nSIMULTANEOUS.\n\n\n==================================================\nSEMIFINAL UI\n==================================================\n\nEach matchup card simply shows:\n\nSEMIFINAL A\n\nBRADLEY\nvs\nALEX\n\n\"Choose/randomize your Rocket League game mode yourselves.\"\n\n\nHost result buttons:\n\nBRADLEY WON\nALEX WON\n\n\nSame for Semifinal B.\n\n\n==================================================\nNO BROWSER DRAW\n==================================================\n\nA bracket match must produce a winner.\n\nIf the player-chosen Rocket League mode ends tied:\n\nThe players themselves must use:\n- Overtime\n- Replay\n- Next scoring event\n- Another mutually agreed deciding method\n\nuntil there is a winner.\n\n\nThen Host submits winner.\n\n\n==================================================\nAFTER BOTH SEMIFINALS\n==================================================\n\nWinners:\nFINAL.\n\nLosers:\n3RD-PLACE MATCH.\n\n\nHost chooses:\n\nSIMULTANEOUS\nor\nSEQUENTIAL.\n\n\n==================================================\nSIMULTANEOUS\n==================================================\n\nBoth match cards active.\n\nEach pair independently chooses its own mode.\n\nThe Final and 3rd-place match do NOT need to use the same mode.\n\n\n==================================================\nSEQUENTIAL\n==================================================\n\nHost chooses:\n\nFINAL FIRST\nor\n3RD PLACE FIRST.\n\n\nOnly active matchup accepts result input.\n\n\n==================================================\nNO FUTURE GAME REVEAL\n==================================================\n\nUnlike Game 85 and Game 86:\n\nThere is no browser-generated future game to hide/reveal.\n\nWhen a matchup becomes active:\nIts players simply decide their mode then.\n\n\n==================================================\nPLACEMENTS\n==================================================\n\nFinal Winner:\n1st\n\nFinal Loser:\n2nd\n\n3rd-Place Winner:\n3rd\n\n3rd-Place Loser:\n4th\n\n\n==================================================\nUNDO\n==================================================\n\nHost:\nUNDO MATCH RESULT\n\nReopens that bracket matchup.\n\nDo not regenerate bracket.\n\nBecause browser does not manage game modes:\nNo mode state needs restoration.\n\n\n=================================================="
