    "tag": true,
    "rules": "==================================================\n\nSUPPORTED FORMATS:\n- 1v1\n- 1v1v1\n- 1v1v1v1 Tournament\n- 2v2\n- 1v2 / 2v1 Tag-Team\n- 1v3 / 3v1 Tag-Team\n\n\nCORE RULE\n\nPlay the native Rocket League Rumble mode for the entire Challenge.\n\nPlayers manually configure Rocket League before gameplay begins.\nThe browser does not configure the Rocket League lobby.\n\nUse the standard Rumble preset / power-up system. Power-ups are part of normal play and remain active through overtime / sudden death.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n1v1\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nMatch Length:\n2 minutes.\n\nUse normal Rumble scoring and gameplay.\n\nHighest score at the end wins.\n\nTie:\nContinue under the same Rumble settings.\nNext valid goal / scoring event wins.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n1v1v1 — THREE-PLAYER ROUND ROBIN\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nBecause Rumble is a two-side Rocket League mode, do NOT try to create a three-team match.\n\nPlay 3 short head-to-head mini-matches so every pairing happens once:\n- Player A vs Player B\n- Player B vs Player C\n- Player C vs Player A\n\nEach mini-match:\n1 minute.\n\nA mini-match win = 1 round-robin point.\nIf a mini-match is tied when the minute ends, continue to the next valid goal / scoring event so that mini-match has one winner.\n\nRank by total mini-match wins.\nIf players are tied in round-robin wins, only the tied players play another deciding head-to-head under the same Rumble settings.\n\nBrowser may use manual placement entry after players finish the round robin.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n1v1v1v1 — TOURNAMENT\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nUse the normal four-player tournament bracket.\n\nSemifinals:\nTwo simultaneous 2-minute Rumble 1v1 matches.\n\nAfter both semifinals resolve:\nWinners play the Final.\nLosers play the 3rd-place match.\n\nFinal + 3rd-place:\nHost chooses simultaneous or sequential.\n\nEach matchup uses the same Rumble rules.\nTie = next valid goal / scoring event.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n2v2\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nMatch Length:\n3 minutes.\n\nPlay normal Rumble 2v2.\nHigher team score wins.\n\nTie:\nContinue under the same mode until the next valid goal / scoring event.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n1v2 / 2v1 — TAG-TEAM\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nKeep Rumble active for the entire Challenge.\n\nSegment 1:\nSolo vs Duo Player A\n1 minute.\n\nSegment 2:\nSolo vs Duo Player B\n1 minute.\n\nAdd the Solo's goals / mode score across both segments.\nAdd the two Duo players' goals / mode score across their segments.\nHigher combined side total wins.\n\nTie:\nBrowser randomly selects one Duo player.\nSolo vs selected player under the same Rumble settings.\nNext valid goal / scoring event wins.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n1v3 / 3v1 — TAG-TEAM\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nKeep Rumble active for all three segments.\n\nSolo plays each Trio member once.\nEach segment = 1 minute.\n\nCombine Solo scoring across all three segments.\nCombine the Trio members' scoring across their three segments.\nHigher total wins.\n\nTie:\nBrowser randomly selects one Trio member for a same-mode sudden-death matchup against Solo.\nNext valid goal / scoring event wins.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nBROWSER\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nThe browser handles:\n- Format / teams / bracket where applicable\n- Tag-Team segment order\n- Result entry\n- Final placements / rewards\n\nThe browser does NOT need to simulate Rumble mechanics.\nPlayers use Rocket League's own mode, score, clock and physics.\n\n=================================================="
